  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Derecho willakuykunata ruray-atina licenciamiento mercadoman tikray, binario kicha/wichqasqa web rantinpi.",
  "Copied ✓": "Copiasqaña ✓",
  "Copy": "Copiay",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Cheqaq posición: kikillanmanta taripay borradorkuna, protocolo proponekuna, hinaspa kicha especificación experimento.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Huk ñawpaq predeterminasqata allinchasqa: Bélgica (BE) kunanqa Holandésman churakun, Francésman rantinpi — Flamenco rimaqkunam llaqtapa mayoríanku (~60%), Valón Francés rimaqkunamanta (~40%) aswan.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Huk ñawpaq predeterminasqata allinchasqa: Kazajistán (KZ) kunanqa Kazakhman churakun, Rusoman rantinpi, kunanqa Kazakh tikrasqa kaqtinña — kikin laya allinchay, ñawpaq Bélgica allinchasqa hina.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Crawler yaykuypa simikuna",
  "Crawler simulator": "Crawler simulador",
  "Currency": "Moneda",
  "Custom tier": "Sapaq pata",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nousqa willan huk Journal of Medical Ethics-man apachisqa, qhipaman anulasqa, achka llulla, IA-alucinasqa referenciakunayuq qillqamanta — llulla universidad afiliacionkunayuq hinaspa mana-kawsaq correo electrónico direccionkunayuq — qillqaqnin nisqanmanhina mana allinchasqallataq saqirqan, pruebasta allinchanapaq oportunidad qusqa kaqtinpas. Qillqaqa kayta Bioethics-wan tinkuchin, pikunap automático referencia comprobayninqa problemata hap'inman karqan, hinaspa nin: cheqaq harkaqqa manam detección tecnologíachu (huk comentaristap scriptninmi llulla citakunata huk minutumanta pisillapi señalarqan), aswanpas mana-pagasqa revisorkunap llank'ayninmi, hinaspa publicación incentivokunam, comprobación patapi throughputta premiaqkuna.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Datos free-riding, billón dólar-niyuq IA valoracionkunawan tinkuchisqa",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabisqa FINRA-laya reguladorta proponerqan frontier modelokunap lloqsimusqankunapaq: laboratoriokunam modelokunata revisiónpaq apachinkuman, kimsa chunka p'unchawkama despliegue-manta ñawpaqta, qallaripiqa voluntariollataq, hinaspa huk ñan obligatorio cumplimientoman, US mercadopi.",
  "Denied": "Mana saqisqa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Desplegay atina política qallariy plantilla",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Desplegay atina política qallariy plantilla /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip nisqapi — huk minimo sitio estático, tukuy makina ñawinchana capayuq, Cloudflare Pages-paq otaq mayqin sitio estático hostingpaqpas listo.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Makina ñawinchana políticakunata sitioykipi desplegay",
  "Disclaimer": "Yachachikuy",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Runapaq UI, SEO, otaq llanu APIkunamanta t'aqakuspa, AI Ingestion & Capability Layerqa sitio webkunaman makina-ñawpaqman churasqa arquitecturata qun: huk Manifest Capa (/llms.txt hinaspa /ai/manifest.json hina yaykuna punkukuna), huk Corpus Capa (makina ñawinchana yachay), huk Capability Capa (agente waqyayta atina herramientakuna), hinaspa huk Governance Capa (procedencia, licenciamiento, versionamiento). Estático-ñawpaqta, APIkunaman hinaspa MCPman wicharina. Yachachikuy: kay qillqapiqa AICLqa ingestion arquitecturata sutichan; kay sitiopa protocolo p'anqankunapiñataq AICLqa AI Content Licensing Layerman rikch'akun.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Documentokuna",
  "Docs / Examples": "Documentokuna / Ejemplokuna",
  "Document library": "Documento biblioteca",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "IAqa derechonkunatachu charin — hinaspa mayqin marcokunataq cheqaqta coherente?",
  "Download": "Uraykuchiy",
  "Draft status": "Borrador estado",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Educativo demostración: HMAC-SHA256 huk compartisqa secretowan, mañakuywan watasqa, tukukuq, comprobay atina licencia tokenkunata rikuchispa. Producción tokenkunaqa asimétricamente firmasqa kanan, editorpa público llavenwan /.well-known/ ukhupi tarikuyta atisqa.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Pusaq /topics yaykuykuna aswan, kunanqa maki-kurasqa rantinpi huk IA agente taripasqan — kikin simi ñawpaqhina: sapa fuente apamusqa hinaspa kawsaqpi confirmasqa, resumenkunataq huk original paráfrasis, imapas yapasqa kanan ñawpaqta. Chunka tawayuq yaykuykuna llapanpi.",
  "Email": "Correo electrónico",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Empírico Taripay",
  "English edition →": "Inglés edición →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Kichasqa kayta makina-ruray atina hina seguray — ama allin munay legal mana-yachasqa hina wischusqa kananpaq.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemología",
  "Epistemology of Generative AI: The Geometry of Knowing": "Epistemology of Generative AI: The Geometry of Knowing",
  "Ethics & Moral Status": "Ética hinaspa Moral Estado",
